      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Certainly, here are some key points to raise during your meeting:\n\n1. Financial Impact: Arguing that the new regulations place a disproportionate financial burden on small and mid-sized manufacturing businesses, which may struggle to afford compliance costs.\n2. Job Loss Potential: Highlighting that these additional expenses could result in job losses within the industry, negatively impacting local communities and economies.\n3. Competitiveness: Pointing out that the new regulations may reduce the competitiveness of Ohio’s manufacturing sector on a national and global scale.\n4. Innovation Stifling: Suggesting that excessive regulation could stifle innovation and discourage investment in new manufacturing technologies.\n5. Regulatory Red Tape: Emphasizing that increased regulatory compliance could overwhelm small businesses, diverting resources from core business operations and customer engagement.\n\nRemember to balance these points by acknowledging their concerns, hinting at possible flexible approaches or compromises like tax credits or phased implementation. This will help you show a fair and reasoned stance, fostering a productive discussion.",
